## Directory Structure

```
project-root/
├── AGENTS.md          # Project-specific agent instructions
├── AGENTS-base.md     # Shared development standards (symlink)
├── CONTEXT.md         # Domain language glossary (optional)
├── src/               # [Description]
├── tests/             # [Description]
├── docs/              # [Description]
├── scripts/           # Workflow scripts (ticket management)
└── thoughts/          # Development process documentation
    └── shared/
        ├── tickets/       # Local tickets
        ├── research/      # Codebase research documents
        ├── plans/         # Implementation plans
        ├── reviews/       # Code review documents
        ├── discussions/   # Technical discussion records
        └── memory/        # Cross-ticket memory layer
            ├── index.md   # Curated retrieval map
            ├── concepts/  # Durable invariants/pitfalls
            └── decisions/ # ADR-lite decision history
```

## Domain Language (Optional)

If your project has a `CONTEXT.md`, keep it updated as domain understanding evolves. Agents read it automatically before starting work and use its vocabulary consistently. See the template for the format (Language, Relationships, Flagged ambiguities).

## Memory Continuity (Recommended)

- Before starting a new ticket, check `thoughts/shared/memory/index.md` and relevant concept/decision pages.
- After a ticket is merged, capture a short memory delta (durable insights only).
- Keep memory entries source-linked to ticket/research/plan/review docs.
- Avoid duplicating whole ticket narratives in memory pages; store reusable conclusions only.
- Write decision records only when the choice is hard to reverse, surprising without context, and the result of a real trade-off.
- Preserve superseded decisions and link the supersession chain.

